q BT 65.20 721.50 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (It was past midnight when Ana heard the gate.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 692.02 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.618 Tw (She had kept the Don's house for twenty years, and she knew every sound it made at night: the) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 671.61 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.663 Tw (old pipes, the wind in the courtyard, the cats on the wall. This sound was none of those. It was) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 651.20 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (the iron gate, swinging open on hinges that should have been locked.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 621.72 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (Ana took the lantern from its hook and went out into the rain.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 592.24 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (A boy stood inside the gate.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 562.76 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.156 Tw (He could not have been more than nine years old. His clothes were wet through, his shoes caked) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 542.35 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.537 Tw (with mud, and he was not afraid. He looked up at the big house the way a boy looks at a house) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 521.94 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (he has seen in a dream -- as if he already knew every window.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 492.46 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("The gate was locked," Ana said. "How did you get in?") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 462.98 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (The boy held up his hand. In his palm lay a rusted key.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 433.50 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("Three, seven, two, nine," he said. "Same as the safe.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 404.02 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.322 Tw (Ana's lantern shook in her hand. She had worked in this house for twenty years, and she had) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 383.61 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.731 Tw (never once heard those numbers spoken aloud. Only the Don knew them. Not even his men) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 363.20 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (knew them.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 333.72 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("Nobody knows that code," a voice said behind her.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 304.24 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.830 Tw (Don Adrian Cole stood in the doorway, his silver hair wet from the rain. He looked at the boy) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 283.83 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (for a long time. Then he looked at the key.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 254.35 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("Nobody knows that code," he said again. "Not even my men. Who are you?") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 224.87 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 2.250 Tw (The boy did not flinch. "My father told me the numbers every night," he said. "He said if) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 204.46 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (anything happened to him, bring the key to the Don.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 174.98 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("Who was your father?" the Don asked.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 145.50 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 2.247 Tw (The boy looked him straight in the eye. "Your driver," he said. "The one who never came) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 125.09 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (home.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 95.61 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (The Don's driver had been gone for three years.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 66.13 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.194 Tw (His name was Frank, and he had driven for the Don for eleven years without a single complaint.) Tj ET Q
