q BT 65.20 771.39 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.592 Tw (Then one night he drove out and never drove back. The car was found the next morning by the) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 750.98 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.116 Tw (river road, empty, the engine cold. No body was ever found. The family said he had run. The) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 730.57 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (Don had never believed it, but he had never been able to prove otherwise.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 701.09 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (Now the driver's son stood in his hall, dripping rainwater onto the marble, holding a rusted key.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 671.61 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("What is your name?" the Don asked.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 642.13 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("Mikey," the boy said.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 612.65 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("Mikey," the Don repeated. "And your mother?") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 583.17 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.699 Tw ("Gone," Mikey said. "Two years now. She told me to wait until I was old enough to walk here) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 562.76 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (alone.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 533.28 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.044 Tw (Ana set the lantern down and put a hand on the boy's shoulder. He was shaking, though not from) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 512.87 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (cold.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 483.39 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("Take him to the safe," the Don said quietly.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 453.91 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.563 Tw (The safe stood behind a panel in the Don's study. It had not been opened in years. The Don) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 433.50 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.496 Tw (turned the dial himself, and when he spoke the numbers, Mikey spoke them with him, word for) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 413.09 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (word, in a small steady voice: three, seven, two, nine.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 383.61 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (The door swung open.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 354.13 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (The Don stared at the empty shelf.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 324.65 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("Something was taken from here," he said.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 295.17 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.402 Tw (It was not a question. Money had been kept in that safe once -- more than any man should keep) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 274.76 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.139 Tw (in a house. And now the shelf was bare, and the Don understood, all at once, that the money had) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 254.35 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.914 Tw (not been spent. It had been taken. By someone who knew the code. By someone inside the) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 233.94 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (house.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 204.46 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.403 Tw (Mikey looked at the empty safe and said, "My father said -- if the safe is empty, only the key is) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 184.05 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (left.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 154.57 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("What key?" the Don asked.) Tj ET Q
