q BT 65.20 771.39 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (his coat still on and told her not to light the lamp.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 741.91 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.291 Tw ("He never said where he drove that night," Ana said. "Only this -- the Don must never know) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 721.50 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (who was in the car.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 692.02 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (The Don looked at Mikey, asleep at last on the couch, the rusted key still clutched in his fist.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 662.54 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("Who was in the car?" he asked.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 633.06 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.615 Tw (Ana shook her head. "He never said. He only said -- if anything happens to me, the boy knows) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 612.65 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (the numbers. The boy knows the key.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 583.17 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (In the morning, the Don took Mikey to the station.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 553.69 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.624 Tw (Mikey led him past the ticket windows and the waiting benches to a wall of small steel lockers) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 533.28 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.157 Tw (at the far end, grey with age, most of them dented and forgotten. He stopped in front of one near) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 512.87 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (the bottom, its lock rusted the same brown as the key in his hand.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 483.39 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg ("My father said -- the truth is behind it," Mikey said.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 453.91 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (The Don knelt, put the key in the lock, and turned it.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 424.43 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.648 Tw (Inside the locker was a single thing: a small tape, in a paper sleeve, with a date written on it in) Tj ET Q
